sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as API identical retry
    participant W as Usage worker
    participant D as PostgreSQL
    Note over A,D: Row selector: customer_billing_state.customer_id = C<br/>Event row: usage_inbox.source = S and usage_inbox.event_id = E<br/>Catalog advisory (65102, 2): protects price_versions, not a column
    alt API holds the usage_inbox row share lock first
        A->>D: BEGIN, duplicate INSERT, compare FOR SHARE<br/>usage_inbox.source = S<br/>usage_inbox.event_id = E
        W->>D: BEGIN, FOR UPDATE<br/>customer_billing_state.customer_id = C, shared catalog lock
        W->>D: Reload the same FOR UPDATE<br/>usage_inbox.source = S<br/>usage_inbox.event_id = E
        Note over W,D: WAIT for the API's usage_inbox row share lock
        A->>D: COMMIT the identical retry
        D-->>W: usage_inbox row lock granted, recheck pending state
        W->>D: Account once and mark processed_at, COMMIT
    else Worker holds the usage_inbox row update lock first
        W->>D: BEGIN, FOR UPDATE<br/>customer_billing_state.customer_id = C, shared catalog lock<br/>Reload FOR UPDATE<br/>usage_inbox.source = S<br/>usage_inbox.event_id = E
        A->>D: BEGIN, duplicate INSERT, compare FOR SHARE<br/>usage_inbox.source = S<br/>usage_inbox.event_id = E
        Note over A,D: WAIT for the worker's usage_inbox row lock
        W->>D: Commit financial effects and processed_at together
        D-->>A: Share lock granted, measurement content unchanged
        A->>D: COMMIT without changing processing state
    end
    Note over A,D: API usage_inbox row does not acquire the customer account lock.<br/>Retry success remains 202 even when accounting completed.
